<title>HONG KONG: China Foods nine-month net HK$23.79 mln.</title>
<headline>China Foods nine-month net HK$23.79 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   4.0	 vs  3.1</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    2.0	 vs  5.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  8.52 loss vs  5.0 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    23.79     vs  17.38</p>
<p>    Turnover		     357.76    vs  626.58</p>
<p>    Company name		 China Foods Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 17-23</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   July 4</p>
<p>NOTE - Food processing concern China Foods Holdings is controlled by China National Cereals Oil and Foodstuffs Import and Export Corp (Ceroil).</p>
<p>The company changed its financial year-end to December 31 from March 31. Comparative figures are for April 1, 1995, to March 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Net is after exceptional loss on provision for diminution in value of interest in short-term investments.</p>
<p>Total dividend for nine months is two H.K. cents vs five (for year).</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
